commit 4c1e8a7d2b9f3065e1a7c8d9b0a1f2e3d4c5b6a7
Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 3 06:20:11 2026 +1000

    Ignore deployer.conf in check-config.sh.
    
    deployer.conf is the configuration file of a containerised deployer
    launcher, a prototype which runs kolla-ansible from a container. It
    lives in the deploy host's configuration directory beside globals.yml
    and is owned by the deploy user rather than being written by
    kolla-ansible for a service.
    
    Like the other deploy host files already excluded here, such as
    globals.yml, passwords.yml and kolla-build.conf, it is not service
    configuration, so skip it when checking file permissions and
    ownership.
    
    Change-Id: I2f6a9d4c7e1b30586a9b0c1d2e3f4051627384a5
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

